WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.600
Welcome to our MAP technical training video. In this video, we'll walk you through the CPL college landing pages,

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.480
what they are, how to customize them, and what the student experience looks like from start to finish.

3
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.280
We'll be using Moreno Valley College during this tutorial.

4
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.720
The CPL landing page is a customizable college specific page that can be posted to your institution's website

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.360
to promote the credit for prior learning opportunities you offer to current and prospective students. Your MAP ambassadors

6
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:35.720
have the ability to personalize this page, including the logo, colors, links, and text.

7
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:43.000
One important thing to note is that once a MAP articulation is fully approved and put into the implementation stage,

8
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:51.120
it automatically displays on this page, so you'll never need to manually update your website every time new CPL is approved.

9
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.040
Now let's look at how to customize your landing page from within MAP.

10
00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.800
We first need to confirm that you have the ambassador role as only ambassadors can customize this page.

11
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.520
You can verify this by checking on the top right hand corner under your name.

12
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.400
You'll be able to hover over your role to see any additional roles as well.

13
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.120
If you do have the ambassador role, we'll go to the main menu on the top left hand corner, select settings, then ambassador.

14
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.600
Once you're in the ambassador module, you'll want to click number three, custom college CPL settings.

15
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.880
This opens the editor page where everything on the left hand side of your screen

16
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.200
represents settings that you can change.

17
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.120
There are three tabs across the top, settings, contacts, and links. The right hand side shows a preview of everything that you're changing.

18
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.600
So let's start with the settings tab.

19
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.200
First, we have the option to select your logo

20
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:53.120
and you can upload it here with any of the accepted file formats. It will display on the upper left hand corner of your landing page.

21
00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:01.040
Below that, we have the custom URL name. Here, you can change the URL name and it'll apply to the very end of the URL.

22
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.480
On this line as well, you can click the link and it'll take you to your live landing page.

23
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.880
You then have the hide logo and hide college name options.

24
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.400
For example, if your logo already has your name on it,

25
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.200
if you want to remove the college name below it, you can, but it's completely optional.

26
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:27.920
Then we have the website text. The website text shows in the drop down below the credit for prior learning on the top of your page.

27
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.240
If a student opens up the drop down, this is the text they will see.

28
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:41.120
Lastly, we have the primary and secondary colors. The primary colors apply to the request CPL review button,

29
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.080
credits, and if you select a star.

30
00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:54.560
The secondary colors apply to the left side navigation links and the top of the cards with the course name within it.

31
00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:01.040
Just be sure to click save changes on the bottom of the screen in order to save any of the updates you may have made.

32
00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.200
Let's move on to the contacts tab. The contacts tab manages who students can reach out to.

33
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.240
At the top, we have the CPL assistant email.

34
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.800
This is the most important field on this tab. When a student selects

35
00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:20.800
request CPL review, their request is sent to that email address. If the field is empty,

36
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.840
then the students will not be able to submit a request and this button will not show.

37
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.400
So just make sure it's filled in.

38
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.200
This can be a shared inbox if you'd like or routed to a specific staff member.

39
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.040
If you want to have additional colleagues to be notified for these inquiries,

40
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.200
you can set that up in the user module by marking student contact.

41
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.160
Please refer to the video managing users and contacts for more information on how to do this.

42
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:53.120
Then we have the website link. You can add your college website to here and it'll go right above

43
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.400
the CPL assistant email on the top left hand side.

44
00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:04.080
Lastly, we have the CPL contacts. In here, you can add new contacts, delete, edit existing,

45
00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.880
or use these three lines to adjust the order of the contacts and they will appear on the left hand side.

46
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.440
If you do any changes here, just make sure to click save changes.

47
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.960
Now let's go to the links tab. You can add new links, edit existing, delete, or again,

48
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.080
you can reorder these in any way you'd like. These show here on the left hand side.

49
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.840
You can see that Moreno Valley has a lot of customized links.

50
00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.800
You can do as many or as little as you would like.

51
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.160
Now let's walk through what the student sees on the live page.

52
00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:45.120
Students can use the search to search for any keywords or they can use any of these filters

53
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:52.240
to browse available CPL courses. They can also toggle between this card view or a list view.

54
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.840
They can export the results that they're looking for with or without filters.

55
00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:04.720
And lastly, they can use these stars to add courses that they're looking to inquire about

56
00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:09.520
and then request the CPL review. When they click the request CPL review,

57
00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:16.000
they'll be prompted to either put in their CCCApply ID or student ID. If they say that they

58
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.760
have neither, then there will be a link to the CCCApply website and they can go from there.

59
00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:26.400
They will also be prompted to fill in their contact information such as first name,

60
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:32.480
last name, email. They can add any documentation or list additional qualifications.

61
00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:39.360
Again, once this request is submitted, it'll send to the CPL assistant email and any additional

62
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:45.600
contacts set up in the user module. One last thing to mention is that once they do request a CPL

63
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:51.600
review, a student profile is automatically created in MAP for you to log in and review the

64
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:57.280
information. This is a full overview of the CPL landing page, how to set it up, customize it,

65
00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.960
and what students will experience when they visit. If you have any questions,

66
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:09.360
please reach out to a customer success manager and we're happy to help.
